# PR review / merge gate

Lesson: [#83](https://github.com/mward-sudo/spec_chum/pull/83) merged with unresolved CodeRabbit threads. Do not repeat that.

## Before merge (agents)

1. Run `./scripts/check_pr_reviews.sh` (paginates GraphQL `reviewThreads`; fails on unresolved bot comments).
2. Treat **CodeRabbit** (and similar bot) comments as blocking when they are **actionable** (bugs, incorrect behavior, clear maintainability fixes).
3. **Do not merge** while actionable bot threads remain unresolved, unless the user **explicitly waives** them (`--waive` / `SPEC_CHUM_REVIEW_WAIVER`, and document the waiver in the PR).
4. Disposition each finding: fix in code, reply with a short wontfix reason, then resolve the thread when GitHub allows.
5. After pushing fixes, wait for a fresh bot pass when practical; address new actionable comments the same way.

CodeRabbit CI status may remain optional; the script is the agent-facing gate (not a brittle required check).

Non-actionable nitpicks may be waived with a one-line reason; do not silently ignore Major/functional findings.
